---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import screenshotImage from '../assets/screenshot.jpeg';
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<main id="landing">
		<div
			class="d-flex flex-md-row-reverse flex-column align-items-center justify-content-center gap-5 p-sm-5 p-3"
		>
			<div class="col-md-5">
				<Image src={screenshotImage} alt="Screenshot of the app showing an example image that says 'Society' on it and it's corresponding label in a text input with three buttons below labeled 'Previous image', 'Export labels file' and 'Next image" class="img-fluid"/>
			</div>
			<div class="col-md-5">
				<h1 class="display-5 fw-bold text-body-emphasis">Labelier</h1>
				<h2 class="lead mb-4">
					A tool that helps you manually label a large amount of
					images for AI training, by making the process as efficient
					as possible, using a simple interface and hotkeys.
				</h2>
				<div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert" hidden id="alert">
					<h4 class="alert-heading">Device not supported</h4>
					<p>
						Labelier uses some features that aren't yet supported on
						your current browser. A solution to this issue is in the
						works. In the meantime, you can use the tool from a
						computer.
					</p>
					<hr />
					<p class="mb-0">
						If you are on a computer and still see this message or
						if you have any other issues, don't hesitate to <a
							href="mailto:adrian@adrianr.dev">reach out</a
						>.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="d-flex flex-sm-row flex-column gap-2">
					<button
						type="button"
						class="btn btn-primary d-none"
						id="load-saved-button"
						><i class="bi bi-folder2-open"></i> Reopen saved directory</button
					>
					<button
						type="button"
						class="btn btn-primary"
						id="load-new-button"
						><i class="bi bi-folder-plus"></i>
						Open new folder</button
					>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="bg-body-tertiary">
			<div class="container py-5">
				<h3 class="border-bottom pb-1">Features</h3>
				<div
					class="row mt-3 row-cols-lg-4 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-sm-1 row-cols-1"
				>
					<div class="col d-flex align-items-start">
						<i
							class="bi bi-wallet2 me-3 text-body-secondary flex-shrink-0 fs-3"
						></i>
						<div>
							<h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 fs-4 text-body-emphasis">
								Free to use
							</h4>
							<p>
								Access all features for free, no purchase or
								subscription neccessary. Forever.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="col d-flex align-items-start">
						<i
							class="bi bi-pc-display me-3 text-body-secondary flex-shrink-0 fs-3"
						></i>
						<div>
							<h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 fs-4 text-body-emphasis">
								Fully local
							</h4>
							<p>
								Runs entirely in your browser, without reaching
								to any external servers. This protects your data
								and your privacy.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="col d-flex align-items-start">
						<i
							class="bi bi-command me-3 text-body-secondary flex-shrink-0 fs-3"
						></i>
						<div>
							<h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 fs-4 text-body-emphasis">
								Hotkeys
							</h4>
							<p>
								Leverage a predefined set of keyboard shortcuts
								and other quality of life features.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="col d-flex align-items-start">
						<i
							class="bi bi-file-earmark-arrow-down-fill me-3 text-body-secondary flex-shrink-0 fs-3"
						></i>
						<div>
							<h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 fs-4 text-body-emphasis">
								Export file with labels
							</h4>
							<p>
								Save a text file with the list of key-value
								pairs of each image name and it's corresponding
								label.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="container mt-5 bg-subtle-secondary">
			<h3 class="border-bottom pb-1">How it works</h3>
			<ol class="list-unstyled vstack gap-3 fs-">
				<li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
					<i class="bi bi-1-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
					<div class="vstack">
						<strong>Load a directory.</strong>
						<span
							>Select a local directory from your computer and it
							will automatically load all images inside it.</span>
					</div>
				</li>
				<li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
					<i class="bi bi-2-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
					<div class="vstack">
						<strong>Label the images.</strong>
						<span
							>The images will appear one by one and in
							alphabetical order by file name. Just type the label
							that you want to set for that image and click save.
							The tool will automatically advance to the next
							image. If you make a mistake or don't want to label
							the image shown yet, you can use the «previous» and
							«next» buttons.</span>
					</div>
				</li>
				<li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
					<i class="bi bi-3-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
					<div class="vstack">
						<strong>Export the results.</strong>
						<span
							>One you've finished labeling all images, click the
							export button and you will be prompted to save a
							text (.txt) file. This file will contain one row per
							labeled image with the format
							<code>image-name.abc&lt;tab&gt;label&lt;lf&gt;</code
							>.</span>
					</div>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</main>
	<footer class="bg-body-tertiary mt-5 pt-3 text-body-secondary">
        <div class="container pt-3">
            <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-md-row border-bottom justify-content-between">
                <p class="col-md-5">If you have any issues, questions or suggestions, feel free to <a
                        href="mailto:adrian@adrianr.dev">reach out</a> so I can improve the app.</p>
                <p class="col-md-5">If you are using Labelier in your company, consider supporting the app by becoming a
                    Sponsor on GitHub.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-center my-3">Made by <a href="https://adrianr.dev">Adrián R</a></p>
        </div>
    </footer>
</Layout>
